                <pb facs="0364" n="282" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg282"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 838.00/592.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the American Minister.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-07-22"><hi rendition="#italic">July 22,
                        1911</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Knox informs Mr. Furniss that the department approves his July 20, noon.
                    Instructs him to persist in the attitude therein indicated and to inform the
                    Government of Haiti that the United States will hold Haiti strictly responsible
                    for any damage that its citizens may sustain as a result of violations of these
                    stipulations.</p>
            </div>
